        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-1331",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "3.1 — Components · Script Compiler",
          "documentation": "Inside script.mjs. A script compiles to an ordinary scenario module rather than being interpreted, so the output stays readable and a flow can be taken over by hand at any point.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1332",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1331"
              },
              "name": "Lexer",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: script.mjs\n\nOne command per line. Strips comments, parses durations such as 2s and 1500ms, splits a trailing within-timeout off a command, and unquotes strings."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1333",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1331"
              },
              "name": "Selector spec parser",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: script.mjs\n\nTurns the button, text and css forms of a selector line into the driver spec strings. A bare value takes the block default, which is why a CSS id needs the css prefix."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1334",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1331"
              },
              "name": "SEL registry",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: script.mjs\n\nNames in the selectors block become slugged keys on the exported SEL map, deduped so two similar labels cannot quietly collide on one key."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1335",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1331"
              },
              "name": "Header parser",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: script.mjs\n\ntarget, app, viewport, match, intro, outro, intro-avatar, outro-avatar and brand. The avatar clip paths are read by cards.mjs, not the driver. An unknown directive is an error naming the file and line, not a silently ignored line."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1336",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1331"
              },
              "name": "Beat parser",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: script.mjs\n\nBeats of wait, click, hover, park, hold, type, press, scroll, open, login, logout, say and if-appears, each becoming one step in order."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1337",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1331"
              },
              "name": "Code generator",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: script.mjs\n\nEmits a scenario module: the SEL map, run(d), and the header exports. Ordinary readable JavaScript, so the generated file is inspectable and hand-editable rather than a black box."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1338",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1331"
              },
              "name": "Ask resolver",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: script.mjs · selectors sidecar\n\nAn ask selector parses to a sentinel spec that travels through the registry as an ordinary string, then gets swapped here for what the sidecar resolved it to. Anything left unresolved is a compile error, never a guess: a guessed selector does not fail here, it fails mid-take with the browser up and the recording started, which is the expensive place to fail."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1339",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1331"
              },
              "name": "Overwrite guard",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: script.mjs · generated marker\n\nRefuses to overwrite a scenario it did not generate; a marker in the header is what tells them apart. Use -o to write elsewhere."
            },
