        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-2380",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "3.6 — Components · Narrator",
          "documentation": "Inside narrate.mjs. The three loudness components are the interesting part: TTS comes back uneven in two different ways, and each needs a different correction applied at a different point.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2381",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2380"
              },
              "name": "Cue file resolver",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: narrate.mjs\n\nReads videoPath out of {take}.recordly to find the cue file belonging to the take that was actually composed, falling back to newest-mtime. Using another take’s cues does not error — it silently narrates over the wrong footage — so the project file, not the timestamp, is the authority."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2382",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2380"
              },
              "name": "TTS gateway",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: tts.mjs · shared\n\nShared with cards.mjs, which is why both stages voice a script identically. Picks the provider, then hits a content-addressed cache keyed by provider+voice+text before spending anything. With DEMO_AVATAR on, the avatar's ElevenLabs voice (DEMO_AVATAR_VOICE) takes precedence over DEMO_TTS and DEMO_TTS_VOICE, so the narration matches the presenter on the cards."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2383",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2380"
              },
              "name": "Breath trimmer",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: tts.mjs · ffmpeg astats\n\nTTS does not start on the word; it starts on 100-160ms at -50 to -85 dB. Cued at the file start that is heard as the line fading up, and normalising a breath just gives a louder breath. Measures RMS in 20ms windows — silenceremove decides on peaks and keeps it — and derives a .lead.mp3 without re-billing."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2384",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2380"
              },
              "name": "Loudness meter",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg ebur128\n\nIntegrated LUFS per clip. Providers do not return lines at a consistent level: measured here, 4.1 LU across one script, worst on the short lines."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2385",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2380"
              },
              "name": "Clip leveller",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg volume\n\nStatic gain to NARRATION_PREMIX_LUFS (-20), capped at ±6 dB, applied per clip before the mix. Static rather than a second loudnorm, which would ride the syllables inside a line. This is the step that cannot be done later: a dynamic pass over the finished mix sets the level of the track, never of a line."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2386",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2380"
              },
              "name": "Overlap checker",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: narrate.mjs\n\nWarns when one line runs into the next rather than letting two clips talk over each other. The fix is a longer hold or a shorter line, both in the script."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2387",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2380"
              },
              "name": "Tail guard",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg tpad\n\nA screencast stops emitting frames when the page stops changing, so a closing line can outlast the video; the last frame is held to cover it. Past PAD_LIMIT_MS that is not a long closing line but the wrong cue file, and the stage throws."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2388",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2380"
              },
              "name": "Mix graph builder",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg filter_complex\n\nPer clip: volume, then adelay to the cue time. Then amix, apad, and the master chain — speechnorm to lift soft line openings, loudnorm to -16 LUFS with true peak under -1.5 dB. Both leave digital silence alone, so the tightener can still find the silent stretches afterwards."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2389",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2380"
              },
              "name": "Muxer",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg\n\nCopies the video stream untouched unless the tail guard needed extra room, so the stage costs seconds rather than a re-render."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClassDiagram",
              "_id": "c4-dgm-2390",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2380"
              },
              "name": "C4-L3 — Components · Narrator (narrate.mjs)",
              "documentation": "Level 3, container \"6 · Narrator\".",
              "defaultDiagram": false,
              "ownedViews": [
                {
                  "_type": "UMLClassView",
                  "_id": "c4-v-2391",
                  "_parent": {
                    "$ref": "c4-dgm-2390"
                  },
