        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-3962",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "3.12 — Components · Publisher",
          "documentation": "Inside publish.mjs. The last step of a video, and the only one that sends it anywhere: gated on the video state and on the explicit approval of the user.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3963",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3962"
              },
              "name": "Publish plan",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: check\n\nThe file and its HD check (ffprobe: at least 1920x1080, H.264 yuv420p), its destinations (PUBLISH_DEST, PUBLISH_YOUTUBE_CHANNEL), the YouTube metadata built from the manifest and the cards (title, description with chapters and contact line, tags, language, privacy, AI disclosure, thumbnail), the ticket, and every reason it may not be published yet: state not done, file missing or not HD, destination or Google credentials not set, YouTube token on another channel."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3964",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3962"
              },
              "name": "Google sign-in",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: auth · OAuth loopback + PKCE\n\nOne-time, once for Drive (auth) and once for the channel (auth youtube): the user signs in in the browser, Google redirects to a 127.0.0.1 port, and the refresh token is written into .env, never printed."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3965",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3962"
              },
              "name": "Approval gate",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: upload --approved\n\nRefuses unless the video state is done (or already published) and --approved is given, which Claude passes only after the user says to publish."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3966",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3962"
              },
              "name": "Drive uploader",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: resumable upload · 8 MB chunks\n\nUploads into the destination folder as the user, or adds a new revision of the file published before so its link stays the same."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3967",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3962"
              },
              "name": "YouTube uploader",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: videos.insert · resumable · 8 MB chunks\n\nChecks which channel the token signs in as (channels.list mine) and refuses unless it is the configured one, uploads the video with its full metadata, then sets the thumbnail (the designed PUBLISH_YOUTUBE_THUMBNAIL image, else the intro title card; a JPEG when over 2 MB). Skips a video already on the channel unless --replace-youtube; thumbnail sets it again later."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3968",
              "_parent": {
